// The same product arithmetic reached through a GENERIC fn. `a * b` gates
// scale's quantified var numeric (NumericGate on the cell); the call
// instantiates the scheme and the copy carries the gate, so binding it to
// `{x: Int}` at the argument edge refuses — at the JUDGMENT, naming `*`'s
// site, with zero WAT. Measured on boot 5bf55b68: compiled, then trapped at
// run time (exit 134) — the twin multiplied two addresses and the field read
// walked off them.
fn scale(a, b) = a * b

fn main() = {
  let p = scale({x: 1}, {x: 2})
  p.x
}
